  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Carter Center -St&#xf6;d till demokratisk styrning och m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Carter Center - Advancing Democratic Governance &amp; Respect for HR/2017-2019</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen ska bidra till att n&#xe5; m&#xe5;len f&#xf6;r Sveriges strategi f&#xf6;r utvecklingssamarbete i DRK 2015-2019 och d&#xe5; speciellt omr&#xe5;det - St&#xe4;rkt kapacitet i det civila samh&#xe4;llet att verka f&#xf6;r &#xf6;ppenhet, ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande och &#xf6;kad respekt f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter. Insatsen uppg&#xe5;r till 30 mkr f&#xf6;r en 3 -&#xe5;rsperiod och Carter Center (TCC) &#xe4;r genomf&#xf6;rare. TCC ska arbeta f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka det civila samh&#xe4;llet i DRK i sin roll att &#xf6;vervaka och rapportera om m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter, gruvn&#xe4;ringen och politiska val samt att ta fram underlag till kampanjer inom dessa omr&#xe5;den. TCC ska st&#xe4;rka civila samh&#xe4;llsorganisationer att n&#xe5; ut till marginaliserade grupper, st&#xe4;rka ungdomsorganisationer samt st&#xe4;rka n&#xe4;mnda organisationers interna kapacitet inom t ex intern styrning och kontroll.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Carter Center (TCC) has applied to Sida for funding of 30 million SEK to carry out the &#x201c; Advancing democratic governance and respect for human rights in the DRC&#x201d; project during the period 2017-2020. 
The intervention aims at :
1) Improved monitoring, analysis, and reporting
2) Enhanced advocacy for reform
3) Increased community engagement
4) Strengthened organisational capacity
The organisation implementing the intervention is The Carter Center. The project is fully financed by Sweden, it is based on TCCs country program, but TCC itself allocates also internal resources for its implementation. Other donors are also funding TCCs work in DRC in similar areas, based on TCCs country program. 
The budget is divided with: 
7 000 000 SEK for the year 2017
13 000 000 SEK for the year 2018
10 000 000 SEK for the year 2019
The project will target Congolese Human Rights CSOs, Young civil society leaders and extractive industries. Sweden has previously supported TCCs work in the DRC with app. 30 MSEK for 2013-2106. An external evaluation of this support was undertaken in 2016 showing positive outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme describes how TCC intends to advance democratic governance and respect of human rights as well strengthen youth political participation in the DRC. It also describes objectives and proposed results, mainly focused on the better understanding of the democratic process, motoring of natural resources, capacity of women and youth leaders and activists to engage in democratic debate and to improve resilience in managing security threats, especially during the electoral period.</narrative>
  </description>
